        "category": "bug",
        "title": "legend_tag mutates caller's attrs dict for required fields",
        "explanation": "The old code always copied attrs via {**attrs, ...}. Now, for tag == 'legend' no copy is made, so attrs is the caller's dict. The following required_css_class branch does attrs['class'] += ..., which mutates the caller's dict. Reusing one attrs dict across calls appends the required class repeatedly.",
        "suggestion": "Always copy: attrs = {**(attrs or {})} and then add 'for' only when tag != 'legend'.",
        "evidence": "attrs = attrs or {}\n                if tag != \"legend\":\n                    attrs = {**attrs, \"for\": id_for_label}",
